Leprechauns in nethack are kind of like ants in the
real world:  there's no such thing as just one of them.
I would say the probability is very high that the
leprechaun you killed is not necessarily the same
one who stole your money.

Leprechauns teleport, so systematically searching
the level does not guarantee you will find all of them.
Leprechaun hunting is a difficult sport.  The only
way I know to be sure you've found them all is to
be telepathic and become blind.  Even then, that
only guarantees you've found all the ones that are
still on the current level; leprechauns are known
to use stairs sometimes, and possibly other means
of getting off-level.

But my advice is, don't worry about it.  Let the
leprechauns run off for now.  They never take
anything but gold, and they're harmless (you
don't get hurt when they attack), so it's safe
to leave some of them alive and go ahead on
to the next part of the dungeon.  Spending a
lot of time hunting down every last one is a
good way to run short on food, so unless
you've got that problem completely sewn
up (large supply, or ring of slow digestion),
I say don't mess with it.  Go ahead and kill
leprechauns as you encounter them, but
if any get away, don't worry about it: let
them get away, for now.

It's not like gold is in short supply.  Unless
you've located an aligned priest and cleared
most of the hostile monsters between here
and there and are actively getting ready to
go and buy protection, you're going to be
finding gold laying around on the floor much
faster than you can find things to do with it.
Gold is by *far* the most plentiful item in the
dungeon.  It's way more common than any
single type of monster and orders of magnitude
more common than any other useful item, even
rocks, even if there are dwarves with pickaxes
digging up every third level leaving piles of
rocks everywhere.  Gold is more common
than all tools combined.  Heck, I think it's
more common than junk armor.  There's plenty.

Besides, sooner or later you'll run into that
leprechaun again just by chance.  Just be
patient; you'll get it eventually.

Nymphs are a different story, as they
sometimes steal things that are much
harder to replace than gold.  IMO,
nymphs are best hunted down and
eliminated as soon as possible.  And
if they drop an unidentified potion
when they die, I #name it with its
random description (bubbly, cyan,
purple-red, whatever), followed by
the word "nymphcount" and a number.
Each time I find a potion in a nymph's
inventory, I increment its nymphcount.
Before long you can be pretty well
certain which potion is object detection.
Collect a big stack of those, and once
you find a co-aligned altar you can
double-dip them in the nearest
fountain and pray for holy water.

(Somebody else said he likes to
quaff potions of object detection
in order to locate vaults, but I have
never had any trouble locating
vaults by more mundane means.
Once you've explored a level
that has vault messages, you
can usually take one glance at
the map and have a VERY good
idea where the vault must be.
Apply a pick-axe, and the gold
that results will buy more divine
protection than half an hour
spent chasing leprechauns.)


